// what it is to a mapper; anywhere after sv_ai_core.qc would compile.
server/monsters/mon_tentacle.qc
// The Xen boids.  Same shape as the tentacle — its own think loop, no schedules —
// and it borrows AI_ApplySequence for the one sequence boid.mdl carries.
server/monsters/mon_flock.qc
// The last boss.  AFTER sv_monsters.qc for monster_alien_slave /
// monster_alien_controller, which MakeFriend calls directly to summon his help.
server/monsters/mon_nihilanth.qc
// NPC test bench.  After the monster files (it names their classes) and before
// sv_player.qc, which dispatches to it from SV_ParseClientCommand.
server/sv_ai_debugcmds.qc
// Posed bodies, not AI — they use Monster_Build but never enter the AI registry.
server/monsters/mon_corpses.qc
// Half-Life's sentences.txt. BEFORE sv_goldsrc_compat.qc, which is where
// scripted_sentence lives and calls into it.
server/sv_sentences.qc
// CTalkMonster: head turn, jaw, idle chatter. AFTER sv_sentences.qc because it
// speaks through it; sv_ai_core.qc forward-declares the two entry points it needs.
server/sv_ai_talk.qc
// scripted_sequence possession. AFTER the whole AI layer (it drives monsters
// through AI_SetSequenceNamed, the path tasks and the schedule gate) and BEFORE
// sv_goldsrc_compat.qc, which used to own the class and now only owns
// scripted_sentence.
server/sv_scripted.qc
// Xen flora (dlls/xen.cpp).  AFTER sv_ai_defs.qc for the ACT_* constants that
// Xen_SetActivity resolves against, and after sh_weapon_standard.qc for
// W_ApplyDamage (forward-declared in the file, but the real one must exist).
// Nothing else depends on it, so its position is otherwise free.
server/sv_xen_flora.qc
server/sv_goldsrc_compat.qc
// Native stand-ins for a map's AngelScript, plus trigger_script (moved out of
// sv_goldsrc_compat.qc).  AFTER that file for GoldSrc_UnknownRelay_Use, which
// trigger_script still forwards through; BEFORE sv_mapcfg_equip.qc, which feeds
// it the cfg's map_script value, and before sv_player.qc, whose PlayerSpawn
// calls MapScript_PlayerSpawn.
//
// th_escape's 17 script functions live in their own file, IMMEDIATELY before
// the registry that dispatches to them — the registry names THEsc_Call,
// THEsc_ResetForMap, THEsc_MapInit, THEsc_PlayerSpawn, THEsc_Frame and
// THEsc_CheckEndConditions directly rather than by forward declaration, so the
// order is fixed.  That file reaches three functions defined later
// (SV_ApplyConfigFile, GoldSrc_GiveByClassname, PlayerApplyModel) by forward
// declaration, and needs no field or constant from any of them.
server/sv_mapscript_thescape.qc
server/sv_mapscript.qc
server/sv_goldsrc_entities.qc
// Sven's trigger_createentity — spawns a child entity at runtime.  AFTER
// sv_goldsrc_entities.qc so the classes it is asked to create are already
// compiled (it dispatches by NAME through isfunction/callfunction, so this is
// about the FGD-visible set being complete rather than about linkage), and
// after sv_multi_manager.qc, whose ED_ParseUnknownEpair harvests its '-' keys
// and whose GoldSrc_TryCaseFoldedField / findentityfield / putentityfieldstring
// it replays them with.
server/sv_trigger_createentity.qc
// The last eleven campaign classnames the 22-map census reported unimplemented —
// the th_ep3_07 ending three (trigger_condition / ambient_music /
// trigger_changesky) plus the cheap stock-HL siblings.  AFTER sv_goldsrc_compat
// and sv_goldsrc_entities, whose helpers and sibling classes it builds on, and
// after sv_trigger_copyvalue (:179), whose DP_QC_ENTITYDATA field-read idiom
// trigger_condition reuses.
server/sv_th_entities.qc
// Opposing Force's emplaced mortar and its two aiming brushes.  AFTER
// sv_th_entities.qc, which owns func_tankrocket: the shell reuses that file's
// CSQC_EVENT_ENV_EXPLOSION convention and W_RadiusExplode call verbatim rather
// than growing a second explosion idiom, and the controller brushes are
// func_tankcontrols' mount/dismount shape with a per-axis latch.
server/sv_op4mortar.qc
// Sven's two co-op progression entities — point_checkpoint (32 placements /
// 16 They Hunger maps) and player_respawn_zone (25 / 14).  Both reuse
// trigger_respawn's relocation shape from sv_goldsrc_compat.qc rather than
// growing a second one; sv_player.qc's half is forward-declared, same as there.
server/sv_checkpoint.qc
// GoldSrc / OpFor / Blue Shift pickups.  AFTER the weapon files (it aliases
// their spawn functions) and after sv_goldsrc_compat.qc, which owns the two
// ammo classes that already worked.
server/sv_goldsrc_pickups.qc
// Stock Half-Life point entities that had no spawn function.  AFTER
// sv_goldsrc_pickups.qc, whose item_antidote / item_security / item_battery /
// item_suit world_items re-enters as; and after sv_sentences.qc (:295), whose
// Sentences_Speak / Sentences_Speaking the speaker announces through.
server/sv_hl_entities.qc
// Counter-Strike point entities — armoury_entity, which is how 1802 of the 1837
// ground weapons in the local CS map corpus are placed.  AFTER the
// shared/weapons/ files (it calls their spawn functions directly rather than by
// classname, so index 13 cannot land on this mod's unrelated weapon_m249), and
// AFTER sv_goldsrc_pickups.qc for GoldSrc_SpawnPickup / GoldSrc_PickupTaken,
// which item_kevlar and item_assaultsuit are built on.
server/sv_cs_entities.qc
// Ammo, on a reserve model: a pickup always takes, and banks what the player
// cannot use yet until they find the matching gun.  AFTER sv_goldsrc_pickups.qc,
// whose GoldSrc_SpawnPickup / GoldSrc_PickupTaken it shares.
server/sv_goldsrc_ammo.qc
// func_healthcharger / func_recharge.  AFTER sv_goldsrc_pickups.qc for
// SUIT_ARMOR_MAX, and BEFORE sv_player.qc, whose PlayerPreThink drives
// Charger_TickInteraction (the held-+use poll, exactly as it drives
// Momentary_TickInteraction).
server/sv_chargers.qc
// Sven's maps/<mapname>.cfg equipment manifest (weapons / ammo / armour),
// which SV_ApplyConfigFile's cvar parser used to drop on the floor.  AFTER
// sv_goldsrc_ammo.qc for Ammo_GiveToCarried and the CAL_* set, AFTER
// sv_goldsrc_pickups.qc for SUIT_ARMOR_MAX, AFTER sv_goldsrc_entities.qc for
// the SF_GPE_* flags and the gpe_item chain fields, and BEFORE sv_player.qc,
// whose PlayerSpawn applies it.  W_GiveWeaponToSlot is forward-declared, the
// same way sv_goldsrc_entities.qc does it.
server/sv_mapcfg_equip.qc
server/sv_ladder.qc
server/sv_cameras.qc
server/sv_trigger_camera.qc
server/sv_trigger_vote.qc
server/sv_spray.qc
server/sv_paint.qc
server/sv_infodecal.qc
shared/sh_pmove.qc
server/sv_grapple.qc
server/sv_player.qc
// Server half of the F5 weapon panel.  AFTER sv_player.qc, which owns
// W_GiveWeaponToSlot / SV_DebugSpawnWeaponId / SV_DebugWeaponOrigin, and after
// sv_goldsrc_pickups.qc, whose 16 alias spawn functions it dispatches by
// classname.  SV_ParseClientCommand lives in sv_player.qc and reaches the
// dispatcher through a forward declaration there — the mirror of
// sv_ai_debugcmds.qc, which compiles BEFORE sv_player.qc and needs none.
server/sv_weapondebugcmds.qc
server/sv_prophunt.qc
server/sv_lagcomp.qc
server/sv_killcam.qc
server/sv_radio.qc
server/sv_bots.qc
server/sv_ragdoll.qc
server/sv_main.qc
